{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;It is not considered the location is suitable for a retail shop. The site is not situated in any of the major/town/neighbourhood centres where commercial development are encouraged. Officers therefore consider the proposed development and its use would appear out of the area&#x27;s character, which is contrary to the following planning policies:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;br&gt;- Policies E9 and SD7 of the London Plan (March 2021);&lt;br&gt;- Policies CM1 and CM5 of the&amp;nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&lt;br&gt;- Policy BE2 of the&amp;nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed retail shop is likely to result in an increased activity level and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance. This is considered to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this residential area and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. As such the proposal is contrary to the following:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023); &lt;br&gt;- Policy D14 of the London Plan (March 2021);&lt;br&gt;- Policies BP8 and BR13 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011); and &lt;br&gt;- Policy DMSI3 of the LBBD’s Local Plan (September, 2024)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reasons of its design and materials, would appear out of the area&#x27;s character, and would not respect the built form of the terrace. As such, the proposed development is contrary to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;br&gt;- Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021);&lt;br&gt;- Policy CP3 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&lt;br&gt;- Policy BP11 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011); and&lt;br&gt;- Policy DMD1 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Plan (September 2024)&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development does not meet the requirement to have a 10% of the Biodiversity Net Gain and therefore would&amp;nbsp;not offer ecological improvements to the site and the surrounding area. As such, it is considered contrary to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as inserted by Schedule 14 of the Environment Act 2021, April 2024);&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;br&gt;- Policies G5 and G6 of the London Plan (March 2021);&lt;br&gt;- Policies CR1 and CR2 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&lt;br&gt;- Policy BR3 of the LBBD&#x27;s&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011);&lt;br&gt;- Policy&amp;nbsp;DMNE3 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Plan (September, 2024)&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
